course: dictionary
lesson: 13173
title: Fragrance: a lovely smell
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A fragrance is a pleasant, sweet smell, like flowers or fresh bread. You can find the meaning by reading the words around it. «The garden was full of roses, and their fragrance filled the air.» The roses are pretty and the air is filled, so fragrance must mean a lovely smell.
explain: A fragrance can also be perfume, or a scent that is added to soap and shampoo. «Mum bought a shampoo with a sweet fragrance.» Here the shampoo has a smell added to it, so fragrance means the scent in the shampoo.
explain: Try swapping in your meaning to check it. «The bakery was full of the fragrance of warm bread.» Put in "smell": "full of the smell of warm bread" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: A fragrance is a pleasant, sweet smell.
fact: Fragrance can also mean perfume, or a scent added to soap, shampoo or other products.
fact: Useful phrases: a sweet fragrance, the fragrance of roses, a fragrance-free soap.
fact: «Fragrance-free» means the product has no added smell.
fact: Some people are allergic to fragrances, so they choose fragrance-free soap and shampoo.
exercise: «The garden was full of roses, and the fragrance made me smile.» What does fragrance mean here? | A cold wind | *A pleasant, sweet smell | A loud noise | A bad smell from the bin
exercise: «The soap has a lovely fragrance of lemons.» Which word tells you the fragrance is nice? | soap | *lovely | has | lemons
exercise: What might «fragrance-free» mean on a bottle of shampoo? | *Has no added smell | Costs less money | Has extra bubbles | Makes your hair smell of flowers
test: «The fragrance of the pine trees filled the forest.» What does fragrance mean here? | A rough path | *A pleasant smell | A tall, green tree | A loud sound
test: Which sense does a fragrance use? | Sight | *Smell | Touch | Hearing
exam: «Some people are allergic to strong fragrances, so they choose gentle soap.» What is a fragrance in this sentence? | A loud sound | *A smell, such as perfume or flowers | A place to sleep | A type of cloth
